From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antonio Sartori <antoniosartori@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:19:06 -0700
Subject: [Permissions] Do not use the visible URL for opaque main frame
 origins

PermissionUtil::GetLastCommittedOriginAsURL() fell back to the
WebContents' visible URL when the primary main frame's committed
origin serialized to an empty URL. However, while a navigation is
pending, the visible URL is the navigation's target and not the URL of
the current document.

Derive the URL only from the committed origin instead. For opaque
primary main frame origins, keep supporting sandboxed documents by
using the precursor origin, which is empty if there is none.

Fixed: 571195939, 571960472, 553148542
Change-Id: If1aaa62234dd4f88fea1bcc83976a362042db208
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8537646
Reviewed-by: Judith Hemp <hempjudith@google.com>
Commit-Queue: Antonio Sartori <antoniosartori@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1716886}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
Context conflict only: this branch's GetLastCommittedOriginAsURL() fallback used web_contents->GetVisibleURL() without DeprecatedGetOriginAsURL(); the whole block is replaced by the upstream logic as in the fix. components/permissions/permission_manager_unittest.cc did not merge and was dropped (test-only; components/permissions is not compiled by Electron).

